<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The river folk (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release C"; DESIGN.md "Rimfolk's peoples"; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/):
    fishers, ferry people and boat-traders who live along the rivers. Medieval, on the game's tribal parent: plain clothes
    and hides of every make, their hats and coats dyed kingfisher blue, river wardens in one kit with fishing spears, archers
    with bows (their kinds, below). Their towns
    are landings by a river (PeopleExtension.byWater: a new world's landings move to a river in reach as the game starts,
    and a new people's is made by one; TownPlanDef Rimfolk_Plan_RiverLanding, its docks laid as a jetty where they reach
    into the water), with fish of the land's own waters in their racks (Odyssey). Their caravans come a little more often
    than another people's (caravanWeight 1.2), with their catch in the stock where the game has fish (Odyssey). A
    boat-trader of theirs brings a catch to the colony's gate (Rimfolk_Evt_RiverCatch, Odyssey); after a hard winter or a
    flood they ask for timber for the boats or cloth for the nets (Rimfolk_Mission_RiverBoats); the flood downriver and
    the ice road come from them likeliest (Patches/Rimfolk_PeoplesC.xml); boatmen of theirs ask to dry and mend their nets
    on the colony's bank (Rimfolk_Evt_RiverNets). Their founding (the description): Wenna Reed's boats, the only ones
    on the water the night the dam broke; a knot in the net for everyone pulled out. What they honour, fear and say is
    in their template (on their card). They defend their landings and raid only when
    the colony has turned them hostile (raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve 0.3). Listed once among the world's peoples when a
    world is made, never required. Faith (Ideology): a fixed creed of the river that feeds them (Alpha Memes' water
    primacy, VE Memes' egalitarian where loaded), the totemic style. Kind of people (Biotech): about four in five baseliners; neanderthals,
    pigskins, yttakin, Stagz Merfolk's coastal merren and now and then one of their abyssal elders come up the river, Alpha
    Genes' nereids, Vanilla Races Expanded's poluxkin and gauranlenkin.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="TribeBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_RiverFolk</defName>
    <label>river folk</label>
    <description>Fishers, ferry people and boat-traders who live along the rivers and know every ford, eddy and shoal of them. Their landings stand where the water is kindest, with docks and fish racks and boats drawn up on the bank, and they carry people and goods across for a price that depends on the weather.\n\nTheir ways began the night the dam broke upriver and the valley towns drowned. The ferrywoman Wenna Reed and her boats were the only ones on the water when it came, and for three days they pulled people off rooftops and carried them to the high bank; those they carried stayed with them. The river folk count their families from that flood, tie a knot in the net for everyone pulled from the water, and on its night carry any stranger across for nothing.\n\nThey talk about the water the way other people talk about family. They are easygoing until someone fouls their water or cheats a ferry, and their river wardens fish with spears that serve for other things. Each landing is kept by its landing master, and the folk by the river master.</description>
    <pawnSingular>river dweller</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>river folk</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>river master</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_RiverFolk</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_RiverFolkTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/RiverFolk</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/RiverFolkTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.06, 0.36, 0.60)</li>
      <li>(0.16, 0.54, 0.80)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>38</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.7</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <allowedCultures Inherit="False">
      <li>Rustican</li>
    </allowedCultures>
    <backstoryFilters Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Tribal</li>
        </categories>
        <commonality>0.5</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Outlander</li>
        </categories>
        <commonality>0.5</commonality>
      </li>
    </backstoryFilters>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.3)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Neanderthal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Neanderthal>
        <Pigskin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Pigskin>
        <Yttakin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Yttakin>
        <Stagz_Merfolk_Coastal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Arquebus.StagzMerfolk">0.05</Stagz_Merfolk_Coastal>
        <AG_Nereid MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.04</AG_Nereid>
        <VRE_Poluxkin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.phytokin">0.03</VRE_Poluxkin>
        <VRE_Gauranlenkin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology,vanillaracesexpanded.phytokin">0.02</VRE_Gauranlenkin>
        <Stagz_Merfolk_Abyssal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Arquebus.StagzMerfolk">0.01</Stagz_Merfolk_Abyssal>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The River's Keeping</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>The river feeds whoever keeps it clean. Take what the water gives and no more, carry the stranger across as the river carried our mothers, and never foul the water another drinks downstream. Everything comes down to the river in the end, and the river takes it to the sea. Whoever is in the water is pulled out first and asked their name after, as Wenna Reed's boats did the night of the flood.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">NaturePrimacy</li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes">AM_WaterPrimacy</li>
      <!-- Whoever is in the water pulled out first: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's egalitarian. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Egalitarian</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
      <Structure_Animist MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">4</Structure_Animist>
      <Structure_TheistEmbodied MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">1</Structure_TheistEmbodied>
    </structureMemeWeights>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Totemic</li>
    </styles>
    <caravanTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_RiverFolk</li>
    </caravanTraderKinds>
    <visitorTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Visitor_RiverFolk</li>
    </visitorTraderKinds>
    <baseTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Base_RiverFolk</li>
    </baseTraderKinds>
    <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <!-- A fight: the river wardens, with fishing spears and bows -->
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>10</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Bowman>8</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Bowman>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher>3</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher>20</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Ferryman>8</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Ferryman>
          <Tribal_Child MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">6</Tribal_Child>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>5</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- A boat-trader's string overland: pack beasts, wardens -->
        <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
        <traders>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_BoatTrader>1</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_BoatTrader>
        </traders>
        <carriers>
          <Muffalo>5</Muffalo>
          <Donkey>4</Donkey>
          <Horse>3</Horse>
          <Alpaca>2</Alpaca>
        </carriers>
        <guards>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>10</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Bowman>8</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Bowman>
        </guards>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>10</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Warden>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Bowman>8</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Bowman>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher>8</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Fisher>
          <Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Ferryman>4</Rimfolk_RiverFolk_Ferryman>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <kindDef>Hunters</kindDef>
        <commonality>1</commonality>
        <options>
          <Tribal_Hunter>1</Tribal_Hunter>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <kindDef>Loggers</kindDef>
        <commonality>1</commonality>
        <options>
          <Tribal_Logger>1</Tribal_Logger>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ColonyCouncil.PeopleExtension">
        <calling>fishers</calling>
        <!-- Their age over the years (Peoples/PeopleAges.cs): an engine for the boats and no more; the river does not change: no further than the industrial age. -->
        <agePace>13</agePace>
        <ageLimit>2</ageLimit>
        <townWord>landing</townWord>
        <townWords>landings</townWords>
        <head>landing master</head>
        <heir>second at the landing</heir>
        <envoy>boatman</envoy>
        <trader>boat-trader</trader>
        <courier>boatman</courier>
        <couriers>boatmen</couriers>
        <caravanWeight>1.2</caravanWeight>
        <camps>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Fishers</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Woodcutters</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_HarvestHands</li>
        </camps>
        <plan>Rimfolk_Plan_RiverLanding</plan>
        <honours>clean water, the stranger carried across and the catch shared</honours>
        <fears>fouled water, a cheat at the ferry and the river rising</fears>
        <sayings>
          <li>Take what the water gives and no more.</li>
          <li>Everything comes down to the river in the end.</li>
          <li>Carry the stranger across.</li>
          <li>Never foul the water another drinks.</li>
        </sayings>
        <townGoods>
          <WoodLog>120~240</WoodLog>
          <Cloth>40~90</Cloth>
          <Pemmican>40~90</Pemmican>
          <MedicineHerbal>4~10</MedicineHerbal>
          <Beer>10~25</Beer>
        </townGoods>
        <ariseAges>0~2</ariseAges>
        <byWater>true</byWater>
        <fish>40~90</fish>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md "Their gear, their kinds of people and their gifts"): river folk vary
    freely around their signature, kingfisher blue on their hats (Ideology's floppy hats, the tuque) and on
    the poncho, coat or cape over their clothes; under it the game's tribal gear and plain trousers, Vanilla Apparel
    Expanded's kilts, ponchos and pelt coats, in their own colours. Their river wardens are their militia and wear one
    kit: the blue tuque, plain clothes, padding where Vanilla Armour Expanded has it, the fishing spear and the game's
    spears and axes; their archers a quiver (Vanilla Apparel Expanded - Accessories). Slings and throwing stones (Vanilla
    Weapons Expanded - Tribal and its base set, Rimsenal's blowguns) and with Vanilla Factions Expanded - Classical fish
    javelins for the fishers. They carry net cloth, herbs or timber, the fishers with Odyssey a catch of river fish, with
    Alpha Crafts a jar of fish sauce. A few are A
    RimWorld of Magic's druids (their river master, now and then a ferry hand) or rangers (wardens and archers). Without
    any mod: tribalwear, parkas, trousers, tuques, the cape, the game's knives, clubs, spears and bows.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_RiverFolkKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_RiverFolk</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.04</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <invFoodDef>Pemmican</invFoodDef>
    <maxGenerationAge>72</maxGenerationAge>
    <apparelTags>
      <li>Neolithic</li>
    </apparelTags>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
      <!-- Kingfisher blue on the hats and the outer coat, whichever they wear. -->
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Tuque</apparelDef><color>(0.14, 0.46, 0.70)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Parka</apparelDef><color>(0.14, 0.46, 0.70)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Cape</apparelDef><color>(0.14, 0.46, 0.70)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology"><apparelDef>Apparel_Flophat</apparelDef><color>(0.14, 0.46, 0.70)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VAPPE"><apparelDef>VAE_Apparel_TribalPoncho</apparelDef><color>(0.14, 0.46, 0.70)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VAPPE"><apparelDef>VAE_Apparel_PeltCoat</apparelDef><color>(0.14, 0.46, 0.70)</color></li>
    </specificApparelRequirements>
  </PawnKindDef>

